course: dictionary
lesson: 6147
title: Millet: a small seed with a big story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Millet is a kind of grass that grows small round seeds. People eat those seeds as grain, in porridge and flatbread. Look for clues in the sentence: «A 4,000-year-old bowl of millet noodles was found at Lajia in China.» Bowl, noodles and found tell you that people made food from millet a very long time ago.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Millet can mean the plant, or the seeds that come from it. In a food lesson it means the seeds. In a pet shop, millet means bird seed. Use the words around it to choose the right meaning.
explain: Millet is uncountable, like rice or sand. You say some millet, not two milets. Try these phrases: millet porridge, and bird seed with millet.
fact: Millet is a grass grown for its small round seeds.
fact: The seeds of millet are eaten as grain by people and by animals.
fact: Millet grows in dry places with poor soil and little rain, so it is an important food crop in parts of Africa and Asia.
fact: A bowl of millet noodles found at Lajia in China is about 4,000 years old.
fact: Millet is uncountable: you say «some millet», not «two milets».
exercise: «A 4,000-year-old bowl of millet noodles was found at Lajia in China.» What does millet mean in this sentence? | *A food made from the seeds of a grass | A tree that grows in China | A kind of pasta from Italy | A type of clay bowl
exercise: Ravi says millet is only for birds. Is he right? | No, millet is a kind of animal | Yes, because millet is a noun | *No, people eat millet seeds as grain, in porridge and flatbread | Yes, millet is only bird seed
exercise: Which phrase shows millet being used as bird food? | *Bird seed with millet | Flatbread with millet | Millet porridge | Millet noodles from Lajia
test: Which sentence uses millet correctly? | We bought millets at the shop. | We bought two millets at the shop. | *We bought some millet at the shop.
test: Why is millet important in dry parts of Africa and Asia? | It needs lots of water and rich soil | *It grows in poor soil with little rain | It only grows in cold places
exam: «Italy already had pasta before Marco Polo.» What does this tell you? | *Pasta was made in Italy before Marco Polo's time | Italy had no food before Marco Polo | Pasta was invented in 1929 | Marco Polo invented pasta
